    "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is a figure in a dark hooded raincoat, standing with their back to the camera.\n<Audio 1> is the voice of <Subject 1>.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] <Subject 1> stands at a rain-streaked window with their back to the camera and speaks one line without turning around.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the figure's coat and posture are retained.\n<Audio 1> (the voice of <Subject 1>): fully_preserved - the voice's timbre, pitch and delivery are retained.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a realistic, full-color cinematic shot with cool grey window light and a shallow depth of field.\n[Shot 1] A medium shot from behind shows <Subject 1>, a figure in a dark hooded raincoat, standing at a tall rain-streaked window in a dim hallway, back to the camera, face never visible. Without turning around, <Subject 1> speaks: (S1) <d>[English] Come in. The door is open.</d> The camera holds steady at shoulder height.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nRain against the window and a faint hallway echo; no other voices.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
