   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 10. Audio to RefCap\nMakes a **voice RefCap** from one sample: the audio is encoded with the H3 audio VAE and saved as `models/refcaps/<name>.safetensors`, holding a single standalone audio reference and no pictures. A short test clip renders at the end. One queue runs it all.\n\n**Steps**\n1. Load the sample in **Your voice sample**. *Load Audio* also reads the audio track of a video file. Use one speaker with no music behind them.\n2. Set the **Trim**. Audio costs 80 tokens per second on every step, and it isn't cut to the render's length. The measured samples were 2.3 s long.\n3. Set `name` on the save node and queue. Refresh the browser so the new file appears in the RefCap lists.\n\n**Using it**\n- Workflow 5 or 6: *Replay View Set* with `audios` = `1`. Workflow 7: chain a *Select* of it, with `audios` = `1`, after the character's own RefCap. Pictures are numbered first and audio last, whatever order the RefCaps are chained in.\n- Bind it in the prompt as the test does: `<Audio 1> is the voice of <Subject 1>.` in `subject_definitions`, a `retention_analysis` line for it, and the words in the shot as `(S1) <d>[English] ...</d>`.\n- The test is fed the trimmed audio directly. That matches replaying the saved RefCap bit for bit, so you can tune the trim before you keep the file. Mute the *Test render* group (select it, Ctrl+M) to skip the test.\n\n**What to expect** (workflow 6's measurements, H3-rendered voices): speaker similarity to the reference was 0.58 and 0.67 with it, and 0.07 to 0.29 without it. Real speakers haven't been tested. A voice identifies a person as much as a face does, so only use voices with consent.\n\n**Settings in these workflows** follow ComfyUI's MiniMax H3 reference-to-video template: the ref2va model with its 4-step Lightning LoRA, 4 steps, `res_multistep` + `simple`, 608x352. For the base model, bypass the *Lightning LoRA* node and use 20 steps. The measurements quoted here ran on a community H3 turbo finetune (shift 6/3, 8 steps) on a 12 GB GPU. Raise the size and length for final renders; the reference tokens ride through every step, so more photos and larger captures cost time."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
