   "title": "Prompt guide",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Writing the prompt\nH3's reference mode reads a structured prompt. The photos are labelled in order: `<Picture 1>` ... `<Picture N>`, where N is the number of photos in the RefCap.\n\n```\nsubject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the woman in <Picture 1>, <Picture 2> and <Picture 3>, a white woman in her mid-twenties with dark brown, wavy, shoulder-length hair.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] <Subject 1> sits at a sunlit cafe table and smiles at the camera.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the woman's facial identity and hairstyle are retained.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a realistic, full-color cinematic shot with warm daylight.\n[Shot 1] A medium close-up shows <Subject 1>, wearing a navy t-shirt, ...\n\noverall_soundscape:\nGentle street ambience.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A\n```\n\n**Tips**\n- Describe age, gender and hair, and **say the outfit and action you want**. The photos supply the face; the prompt supplies everything else.\n- Don't count on a name. The tests never used one.\n- More detail in `detailed_description` (camera, lighting, motion, sound) gives better shots. MiniMax's guide suggests 350-500 words for final renders.\n- Official format guide: MiniMax-H3 `docs/VIDEO_PROMPT_WRITING_GUIDE_ref_en.md`."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
